{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Upon me your curse.</b> Do not fear lest he curse, and if he curses, let his curse be upon me and not upon you. And this is the plain sense of the words. And the Gaon [Saadia] interpreted עלי as 'to remove your curse.' And some say, heaven forbid that the prophet should deceive — rather it was so:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "Resolved the abbreviated epithet והגאון as the Gaon [Saadia], the standard identification in Ibn Ezra's commentary."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:59.747997994Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}